Package: CohortHonestDiD
Type: Package
Title: Cohort-Anchored 'HonestDiD' Sensitivity Analysis for Staggered Adoption
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(person("Ziyi", "Liu", email = "zyliu2023@berkeley.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")), person("Ashesh", "Rambachan", role = "ctb", comment = "Upstream HonestDiD inference routines"), person("Jonathan", "Roth", role = "ctb", comment = "Upstream HonestDiD inference routines"))
Description: Performs cohort-anchored sensitivity analysis for
    difference-in-differences designs with staggered adoption, as proposed
    by Liu (2026) "Cohort-Anchored HonestDiD" <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2509.01829>. The
    restrictions of Rambachan and Roth (2023) <doi:10.1093/restud/rdad018>
    are placed on each cohort's block bias, its untreated trend relative to
    the units untreated when the cohort first adopts treatment, and a known
    linear map carries block biases into the biases of the estimated
    coefficients. Estimates imputation and Callaway-Sant'Anna cohort-period
    effects with their joint covariance. Provides relative-magnitude and
    smoothness restrictions, conditional and conditional least-favorable
    confidence sets, fixed-length intervals, and aggregate benchmarks.
